    "created_at": "2026-01-05T08:16:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T08:16:33Z",
    "body": "No strong opinions here. My suggestion to use microseconds was mainly driven by API consistency. The `expires` attribute is defined as a `DOMHighResTimeStamp`, which is expressed in milliseconds. If `maxAge` is instead expressed in seconds, the two attributes end up having different precision and expressivity, despite representing closely related concepts.",
